Patch 6008: immediate-mode (register-based) vertices reach the live renderer (rc-RE pass 19-20, found with patch
6007's RSX_BE_LOG on run tods-be-log). Tools of Destruction's main menu draws its Bink movie background as BEGIN QUADS,
one DATA4UB colour (attr2), then per vertex DATA2F attr1, DATA2F attr3 and DATA2F attr0 (position) last; the live
renderer drew nothing for these groups.
rsx_dispatch.c: vtx_attr0_completes(): the last word of ATTR0 in every SET_VERTEX_DATA* format completes a vertex
(DATA1F 0x1E40, DATA2F 0x1884, DATA3F 0x1508, DATA4F 0x1C0C, DATA2S 0x1900, DATA4UB 0x1940, DATA4S 0x1984,
DATA_SCALED4S 0x0A84), not only DATA3F z and DATA4F w. RPCS3 [rsx_vertex_data.cpp get_vertex_id] counts a vertex once
ATTR0 has all the dwords of its format.
rsx_live_draw.c: sink.immediate_vertex: one ATTR0..15 snapshot per vertex (growable, 4096 cap: a larger group is
logged and not drawn, never a truncated prefix), drawn at END through the ordinary path (compact or legacy payload,
same topology rebuild, PSO and textures); not in the vertex payload cache, never GPU-fetched. A group that also has
array/index/inline batches draws the batches as before and leaves the immediate vertices out (logged; RPCS3 uses the
push-buffer count only when no draw command was set). Tests: test_rsx_immediate_vertex (host, CI), a DATA2F quad in
test_rsx_draw_engine, test_live_draw_immediate_quads (Windows D3D12). General; upstream only with the PM's OK.

